  "followup_backlog_text": "## aminx #1981: AR decoder loop-body scaling (loop_body_scales finding)\n\nlayer_b_loop_cost.py (T7) measured the AR decode kernel's while-loop body_operand_elements scaling alpha (L=256->512) above the 0.35 bar under `incremental=\"force\"`, meaning the per-wave loop body carries data-flow weight that grows faster than expected for a supposedly O(1)-per-wave incremental cache. Top offending body instructions (by weight): bitcast_dynamic-slice_fusion.2, bitcast_dynamic-slice_fusion, select_dynamic-update-slice_fusion, bitcast_select_fusion.2, bitcast_select_fusion.1. Needs investigation of what in the incremental decode path (KV-style cache update, position-map gather, or fixed-mask broadcast) scales with L instead of the wave size.",
